// Spec: 06-types.md § Derive — Debug on a distinct-outer-generic receiver (ROOT A)
// Formal semantics: a derived `debug` must be emitted for every concrete instantiation
// a call site can demand, including an inner instantiation reachable ONLY through a
// distinct outer generic's field (`Outer<Inner<int>>` -> inner `Inner<int>`). The
// inner-only `Inner<int>` instantiation STARVES on the AOT (LLVM) backend with
// "unresolved function `debug` in apply — missing mono instance?", while the
// interpreter (the parity oracle) produces the structural string correctly.
//
// TDD-first: this cell FAILS pre-fix on the LLVM backend (missing mono
// instance) and PASSES on the interpreter. ISOLATION + SHAPE: the non-emptiness gate
// `a.debug() != ""` HARD-FAILS pre-fix; an exact-string `assert_eq` would mask it (see
// derive_nested_generic_debug.ori). The exact-string parity pin (`Outer { y: Inner {
// x: 3 } }`) is the implementation work_item's post-fix verification.

use std.testing { assert }

#[derive(Eq, Hashable, Debug)]
type Inner<T> = { x: T }

#[derive(Eq, Hashable, Debug)]
type Outer<T> = { y: Inner<T> }

@test_two_generic_debug tests @two_debug () -> void = {
    let a = Outer { y: Inner { x: 3 } };
    assert(cond: a.debug() != "")
}
@two_debug () -> str = {
    let a = Outer { y: Inner { x: 3 } };
    a.debug()
}
